menuconfig HRM
    bool "Heart Rate Monitor"
    help
      Heart Rate Monitor Drivers

if HRM

config HRM_GH3X2X
    bool "Goodix GH3X2X"
    help
      Support for the Goodix GH3X2X heart rate sensor.

config HRM_AS7000
    bool "ams AS7000"
    depends on SOC_STM32F4
    help
      Support for the ams AS7000 heart rate sensor of the Pebble 2 HR. Uses
      the application already in the sensor flash and reports heart rate
      only. The sensor is probed at boot, so the Pebble 2 SE runs the same
      firmware.

config HRM_AS7000_HRV
    bool "AS7000 HRV (PRV application)"
    depends on HRM_AS7000
    select HRM_HRV
    help
      While an app asks for HRV, ask the sensor to run its undocumented PRV
      (pulse rate variability) application next to HRM, as the Pebble
      Time 2 runs HRV only while an app asks. Falls back to HRM alone if
      the sensor does not start with PRV. Never writes the sensor flash.
      With PRV running the LEDs pulse too fast to see flicker, so they
      look solid. Apps get no HRV data yet: the PRV results are not
      decoded.

config HRM_AS7000_PRV_PROBE
    bool "AS7000 PRV probe (diagnostic)"
    depends on HRM_AS7000_HRV
    help
      Record the registers around the PPG block at each handshake, for
      Settings > System > Information and app logs, to work out the PRV
      results. The Information row can also ask for HRV itself.

config HRM_SPO2
    bool
    default y if HRM_GH3X2X || HRM_QEMU
    help
      The sensor measures blood oxygen (SpO2). Without it the blood oxygen
      settings are neither shown nor synced with the phone, and the HRM
      manager never asks for SpO2.

config HRM_HRV
    bool "HRV (RR interval) support"
    depends on HRM_GH3X2X || HRM_AS7000_HRV
    default n
    help
      Expose heart-rate-variability (RR/inter-beat interval) data from the
      HRM sensor. On the GH3x2x, enables the Goodix HRV algorithm and links
      the nonfree HRV library. Off by default; HRV is only sampled while an
      app holds an HRV subscription.

config HRM_QEMU
    bool "QEMU"
    default y if SOC_QEMU
    help
      QEMU heart rate monitor. QEMU emulates none, so it can be enabled
      but never delivers samples.

module = DRIVER_HRM
module-str = Heart Rate Monitor
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_level"

endif # HRM
